  {
   "id": "S6",
   "text": "You hear AI, machine learning, deep learning, generative AI, and sometimes all in the same conversation. And you might be thinking, \"Are these just different names for the same thing?\" They're definitely related, but they mean different things. Once you understand the difference, you can start understanding what the tool you're using actually does. So what's the difference between rule-based clinical system? And how machine learning actually learns from the patterns of the patient's history and how it can predict the hospitalization risk and how deep learning can actually save our patients? All of that I'll be explained in my video on my page. So next time, somebody says to you, \"We use AI, it doesn't tell you much.\" You ask, \"Okay, show me what it does in my working day.\"",
